<title>INDIA: India's VSNL 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India's VSNL 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	  5,030.0   vs     4,088.0</p>
<p>    Net sales	  51,944.0   vs    44,343.0</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	62.88  vs	  51.1</p>
<p>    Other income	  683.0   vs	 388.0</p>
<p>    Expenditure	43,603.0   vs    37,168.0</p>
<p>    Interest costs	 40.0   vs	  67.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  674.0   vs	 558.0</p>
<p>    Tax		   3,280.0   vs     2,850.0</p>
<p>    Gross profit	8,984.0   vs     7,496.0</p>
<p>Note: Videsh Sanchar Nigam Ltd (VSNL), India's telecom giant, said the earning per share for the year ending March 31, 1997 has been calculated on the pre-Global Depository Issue (GDR) capital base.</p>
<p>The firm made a GDR issue of 12.16 million additional shares at a value of 1,000 rupees in March against a face value of 10 rupees per share.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
